## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic synchronization primitives and common OS patterns, especially producer-consumer, deadlock avoidance, and correct semaphore/mutex usage in C.

## Key Concepts
- Semaphores
- Mutex
- Circular buffer
- Deadlock detection
- Boundary conditions (full/empty)

## Code Example
```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <semaphore.h>
#include <stdio.h>

#define N 10

int buffer[N];
int in = 0, out = 0;
sem_t empty, full;
pthread_mutex_t mutex;

void produce(int item) {
  sem_wait(&empty);
  pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);
  buffer[in] = item;
  in = (in + 1) % N;
  pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
  sem_post(&full);
}

int consume() {
  int item;
  sem_wait(&full);
  pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);
  item = buffer[out];
  out = (out + 1) % N;
  pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
  sem_post(&empty);
  return item;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to multiple producers/consumers and ensure fairness?
- What are trade-offs vs. using condition variables instead of semaphores?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of memory cache eviction with per-process quotas, correctness under concurrency, and interaction with remote backends.

## Key Concepts

- Per-process quotas and accounting
- Per-page state (clean/dirty, eviction-claimed, evicted) and CAS-based races
- Eviction flow: candidate selection, quota enforcement, writeback coordination
- Data structures: per-CPU LRU, global eviction gate, writeback queues
- Remote store latency impact and fairness guarantees

## Code Example

```c
// Minimal eviction sketch
typedef struct page {
  atomic_int ref;
  int owner;                  // pid
  atomic_bool dirty;
  atomic_bool evicted;
  atomic_bool claimed;
} page_t;

bool evict_candidate(page_t *p, int owner_quota) {
  if (atomic_load(&p->dirty)) return false;      // never evict dirty before writeback
  if (atomic_load(&p->claimed)) return false;    // another thread claiming it
  if (atomic_compare_exchange_strong(&p->claimed, 0, 1)) {
    // update owner quota here atomically (pseudo)
    atomic_store(&p->evicted, 1);
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

